{"base_rate":0.6824644549763034,"brier":0.21161263823064774,"bss":0.023506813156439765,"bss_hi":0.1234251579822022,"bss_lo":-0.08282770764269007,"chart":{"base":[652.0,240.3],"fp":[684.6,295.0],"note":{"base":"skill 0.02 — higher than 12% of cities","fp":"low end +30pp, high end +6pp","rel":"promised 15% → rained 46%; promised 98% → rained 86%"},"rel":"153.9,268.7 368.1,213.1 507.1,160.9 605.2,121.1 680.3,94.8"},"country":"VC","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.12849921011058454,"ess":466.45320038597555,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Kingstown</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Kingstown rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>93%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(6%), there is still roughly a <b>36%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 633 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-24. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 8.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.02, ranked 190 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(171&ndash;199) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>6%</td><td class='num'><b>36%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>23%</td><td class='num'><b>55%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>41%</td><td class='num'><b>52%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>56%</td><td class='num'><b>65%</b></td><td class='num'>62</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>67%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>75%</td><td class='num'><b>79%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>74%</b></td><td class='num'>57</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>89%</td><td class='num'><b>85%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>96%</td><td class='num'><b>79%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>93%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 10 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Kingstown</b> <span class=\"muted\">Saint Vincent and the Grenadines</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;68% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 68% of days.</p><p>The forecast did only slightly better. The difference is within the margin of error.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.02</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>171&ndash;199\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>633 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Kingstown &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Kingstown\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"77.67311475409836,340.2295081967213 139.1518181818182,260.6666666666667 202.61770491803279,185.08196721311475 256.98225806451603,135.4193548387097 293.43809523809523,98.88888888888886 322.71333333333325,70.0 349.46000000000004,49.92982456140351 374.0925,33.16666666666663 398.8845901639343,18.0 411.3659701492537,18.0 411.3659701492537,23.432835820895548 398.8845901639343,47.8360655737705 374.0925,83.72222222222223 349.46000000000004,120.17543859649123 322.71333333333325,150.8888888888889 293.43809523809523,185.55555555555557 256.98225806451603,223.48387096774192 202.61770491803279,280.55737704918033 139.1518181818182,332.3636363636364 77.67311475409836,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"133.58293838862556\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"133.58293838862556\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"77.67311475409836,250.72131147540983 139.1518181818182,183.45454545454547 202.61770491803279,191.04918032786884 256.98225806451603,147.16129032258064 293.43809523809523,156.66666666666666 322.71333333333325,93.11111111111114 349.46000000000004,113.78947368421052 374.0925,73.61111111111114 398.8845901639343,95.57377049180326 411.3659701492537,45.164179104477626\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 6%&amp;#10;It rained 36% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 61 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"77.67311475409836\" cy=\"250.72131147540983\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 23%&amp;#10;It rained 55% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"139.1518181818182\" cy=\"183.45454545454547\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 41%&amp;#10;It rained 52% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 61 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"202.61770491803279\" cy=\"191.04918032786884\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 56%&amp;#10;It rained 65% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 62 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"256.98225806451603\" cy=\"147.16129032258064\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 67%&amp;#10;It rained 62% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 63 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"293.43809523809523\" cy=\"156.66666666666666\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 75%&amp;#10;It rained 79% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 63 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"322.71333333333325\" cy=\"93.11111111111114\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 82%&amp;#10;It rained 74% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 57 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"349.46000000000004\" cy=\"113.78947368421052\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 89%&amp;#10;It rained 85% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"374.0925\" cy=\"73.61111111111114\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 96%&amp;#10;It rained 79% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 61 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"398.8845901639343\" cy=\"95.57377049180326\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 93% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.3659701492537\" cy=\"45.164179104477626\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(68%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Kingstown the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>summer</b> (0.03) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (-0.03).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>170</td><td class='num'>75%</td><td class='num'>-0.029</td><td class='num'>11.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>144</td><td class='num'>60%</td><td class='num'>-0.028</td><td class='num'>15.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>160</td><td class='num'>59%</td><td class='num'>0.006</td><td class='num'>14.9%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>159</td><td class='num'>77%</td><td class='num'>0.026</td><td class='num'>9.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":13.15527,"lon":-61.22742,"n":633,"n_cities":216,"name":"Kingstown","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.14,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.05557377049180328,"n":61,"obs":0.36065573770491804,"sig":true},{"hi":0.3180000000000001,"lo":0.14,"mean":0.22924242424242425,"n":66,"obs":0.5454545454545454,"sig":true},{"hi":0.49,"lo":0.3180000000000001,"mean":0.4085245901639344,"n":61,"obs":0.5245901639344263,"sig":false},{"hi":0.63,"lo":0.49,"mean":0.5620967741935482,"n":62,"obs":0.6451612903225806,"sig":false},{"hi":0.71,"lo":0.63,"mean":0.6650793650793652,"n":63,"obs":0.6190476190476191,"sig":false},{"hi":0.8,"lo":0.71,"mean":0.7477777777777775,"n":63,"obs":0.7936507936507936,"sig":false},{"hi":0.86,"lo":0.8,"mean":0.8233333333333334,"n":57,"obs":0.7368421052631579,"sig":false},{"hi":0.94,"lo":0.86,"mean":0.8929166666666666,"n":72,"obs":0.8472222222222222,"sig":false},{"hi":0.99,"lo":0.94,"mean":0.9629508196721309,"n":61,"obs":0.7868852459016393,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.99,"mean":0.9982089552238805,"n":67,"obs":0.9253731343283582,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":8.5,"provisional":false,"rank":190,"rank_hi":199.0,"rank_lo":170.975,"reliability":0.026249026104472554,"resolution":0.026755812177812914,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"kingstown","station":"","timezone":"America/St_Vincent"}